+
+/**
+ * Source-engine style launch commands: `+name arg arg` groups collected by
+ * Init() from the positional arguments, in the order they appeared. Each entry
+ * is one console line ("name arg arg"), ready to hand to a console executor.
+ *
+ * These are deliberately NOT applied by the cvar layer. A `+map` has to run
+ * after the app is up, and only the app knows when that is - so Init() only
+ * collects them and the app drains them at a point of its choosing.
+ *
+ * Takes: the queue is cleared, so a second call returns empty.
+ */
+std::vector<std::string> TakeLaunchCommands();
